  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 129 AM EDT Sat Sep 26 2026\n\nIn the upper levels, a ridge is over the Mississippi Valley and a \nclosed low is just off the coast of the Mid-Atlantic. At the \nsurface, high pressure is centered over the Great Lakes extending \nsouthward to the Gulf Coast. A Nor'easter is just off the coast of \nthe Mid-Atlantic. Dry, sunny weather with pleasant temperatures will \ncontinue this weekend and into early next week with highs mainly in \nthe 70s.  \n\nBy midweek, the pattern starts to change with a weak ridge over the \nSoutheast and a closed low developing over the Southwest. A warming \ntrend will become noticeable by Tuesday or Wednesday with highs in \nthe 80s for the rest of the workweek. Some low rain chances are in \nthe forecast for Thursday and Friday to account for uncertainty but \nit looks like the system will move northeast into the Midwest late \nin the workweek.",
